(*  Isabelle session for the WEV-SMT mechanisation (TACAS 2027 artifact).

    Build with:   isabelle build -d . WEV_SMT WEV_SMT_PwT
    Verbose:      isabelle build -d . -v WEV_SMT WEV_SMT_PwT
    Force rerun:  isabelle build -d . -c WEV_SMT WEV_SMT_PwT

    Two sessions. WEV_SMT holds the original abstract development (Lemma 2,
    detector exactness, Theorem 1). WEV_SMT_PwT, in the pwt/ subdirectory,
    holds the PwT correspondence: the BV32 expression language, the concrete
    constancy predicate, the model that discharges WEV_SMT's abstraction, the
    per-site R4b results and the program-level lifting. They are separate
    sessions because Isabelle does not permit two sessions to share a source
    directory, and because only the second needs HOL-Library.Word.

    Depends on HOL and HOL-Library only; no AFP entries are used.
*)

session WEV_SMT = HOL +
  description \<open>
    Mechanisation of Lemma 2 (detector soundness), the branch-free detector
    exactness result, and Theorem 1 (WEAKEST consistency rules out thin-air
    cycles) for the WEV-SMT semantic-dependency checker.
  \<close>
  options [document = false]
  theories
    WEV_SMT_Defs
    Detector
    Soundness

session WEV_SMT_PwT in "pwt" = WEV_SMT +
  description \<open>
    Mechanisation of the PwT correspondence: the 32-bit branch-free expression
    language of the QF_BV constancy oracle, the per-site equivalence between
    PwT's two-point R4b check and non-constancy, and the program-level
    over-approximation result for WEAKEST's composed semantic dependency.
  \<close>
  options [document = false]
  sessions
    "HOL-Library"
  theories
    PwT_Expr
    PwT_Constancy
    PwT_Model
    PwT_R4b
    PwT_Program
